# PayloadCMS Implementation Guidelines

<rule>
name: atlas_payloadcms
description: Standards for implementing proper PayloadCMS applications and patterns
filters:
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "payload/"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)payloadcms|payload cms|collection|field|access control"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When implementing PayloadCMS code:

      ## Collections
      - Use proper collection structure
      - Implement proper field definitions
      - Use proper validation rules
      - Access control is handled by a plugin, but may be overwritten in special cases
      - Follow collection best practices

      ## Fields
      - Use proper field types
      - Implement proper relationships
      - Use proper field validation
      - Implement proper conditional fields
      - Follow field best practices

      ## Access Control
      - Implement proper user roles
      - Use proper document-level access
      - Implement proper field-level access
      - Use proper authentication strategies
      - Follow access control best practices

      ## Hooks
      - Use proper beforeChange hooks
      - Implement proper afterChange hooks
      - Use proper beforeRead hooks
      - Implement proper afterRead hooks
      - Follow hook best practices

      ## Admin UI
      - Implement proper admin components
      - Use proper field customization
      - Implement proper layout customization
      - Use proper custom views
      - Follow admin UI best practices

examples:
  - input: "Creating a new PayloadCMS collection"
    output: "Collection includes proper fields, validation, access control, and follows PayloadCMS best practices"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule> 